+## v1.2.43.2.3 - Clean export patches exclusion hotfix
+
+- Fix the clean exporter so the documented `patches/` exclusion is actually passed to `zip`; previous v1.2.43.2.x exports could still include the historical patch archive even though `EXPORT_INDEX.md` claimed it was omitted.
+- Make `make export` itself fail closed when any forbidden runtime/generated entry survives filtering, printing up to 20 offending paths instead of relying only on the later `export-check` gate.
+- Preserve the v1.2.43.2.1 EOF-consuming pipeline behavior, size/entry/SHA-256 logging and the v1.2.43.2.2 deterministic project-explorer test.
+
 ## v1.2.43.2.2 - Project explorer async test stabilization
 
 - Fix the AgentWorkspace project-explorer regression to wait for the asynchronously loaded `README.md` tree item itself instead of waiting on the always-present refresh control.
diff --git a/VALIDATION.md b/VALIDATION.md
index d54142ccc3f3155dd824a175b0a50818d4413a67..d9c10336a789fe74a71e82b7d06f346cb5e94a52 100644
--- a/VALIDATION.md
+++ b/VALIDATION.md
@@ -1,3 +1,10 @@
+## v1.2.43.2.3 clean export patches exclusion regression
+
+- Reproduced from the operator run after v1.2.43.2.2: application/frontend/Desktop gates pass, `make export` produces an archive, then `export-check` rejects it because `patches/` is still present.
+- Root cause: `scripts/export.sh` documented `patches/` as excluded but its `zip -x` pattern list omitted both `patches/` and `patches/*`.
+- The exporter now excludes the whole historical patch tree and performs the forbidden-entry scan itself before publishing the archive, with bounded offending-path diagnostics.
+- Required regressions: `make export` must produce no `^patches/`, `.harness`, `.idea`, `.orig/.rej`, `kernl-context-*`, `wharness-input-*` or `wharness-bundle-*` entries; `make export-check` must pass; final export must retain path/size/entries/SHA-256 logging.
+
 ## v1.2.43.2.2 project explorer async regression
 
 - `AgentWorkspace` project-explorer coverage waits for the `README.md` file button returned by the mocked asynchronous `api.listFiles()` call before clicking it.
diff --git a/scripts/export.sh b/scripts/export.sh
index 97f01a139b1ba40841eb049090721381c28093ea..104ae55ec53c0a7d3e93814e38c7afe0ebeb707a 100755
--- a/scripts/export.sh
+++ b/scripts/export.sh
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ archive="$tmp_dir/wharness.zip"
 
 excludes=(
   '.git/*' '.env' 'EXPORTS.md' 'EXPORT_INDEX.md'
+  'patches/' 'patches/*'
   '.harness/*' '*/.harness/*' '.idea/*' '*/.idea/*'
   'node_modules/*' '*/node_modules/*' 'dist/*' '*/dist/*'
   'build/*' '*/build/*' 'coverage/*' '*/coverage/*'
@@ -65,6 +66,16 @@ source_bytes="$(unzip -l "$archive" | awk 'END {print $1+0}')"
   zip -q wharness.zip EXPORTS.md EXPORT_INDEX.md
 )
 
+forbidden_entries="$tmp_dir/forbidden-entries.txt"
+unzip -Z1 "$archive" | awk '
+  /(^|\/)\.harness\// || /(^|\/)\.idea\// || /^patches\// || /\.(orig|rej)$/ || /(^|\/)(kernl-context-|wharness-input-|wharness-bundle-)/ { print }
+' > "$forbidden_entries"
+if [[ -s "$forbidden_entries" ]]; then
+  echo "export contains forbidden runtime/generated entries:" >&2
+  awk 'NR <= 20 { printf "  - %s\n", $0 } END { if (NR > 20) printf "  ... and %d more\n", NR-20 }' "$forbidden_entries" >&2
+  exit 1
+fi
+
 mv -f "$archive" "$EXPORT_ARCHIVE"
 test -s "$EXPORT_ARCHIVE"
 unzip -tqq "$EXPORT_ARCHIVE"
